The two full-suite failures are pre-existing on the manus-parity lineage and are not
caused by H2 (neither file is in this diff, and both reproduce identically on
manus-parity):
1. `src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` -> "keeps every coding-profile tool
   either linted or explicitly pending". The inherited D4 defect: `suggest_plan` is in
   `CODING_PROFILE.tools` but not in the test's `PENDING_CODING_TOOLS`, and the test's
   registry does not include `createPlanTools`.
2. `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> "reports non-git folders without
   throwing". Environmental: `%TEMP%` sits inside a git repository on this machine, so
   `git rev-parse` in a plain temp folder succeeds and `isGit` reports true.

No test was weakened, deleted or skipped. No secrets committed. No forbidden path
touched (`docs/handoff/watchdog.ps1`, `qa/*.png`, `packages/tests/visual/baselines`,
ZCode/Codex files). Arabic was written only through the file tool; the fixture
`"لا، قلت لك اكتب الاسم بالعربي"` is stored as valid UTF-8 (verified byte-level, no
`???` or U+FFFD). The pre-existing uncommitted `deleted: .jdone` from the worktree
setup was left untouched and is not part of this commit.

